      "message": "validation: make package transactions trimmed after submission reconsiderable\n\nA transaction evicted by LimitMempoolSize() right after being accepted\nby itself is TX_RECONSIDERABLE: a package with a higher feerate may\nstill get it in. Transactions submitted together as a package and\nevicted by the final trim in AcceptPackage() were TX_MEMPOOL_POLICY\ninstead, as that code predates TX_RECONSIDERABLE.\n\nFor 1p1c relay this put an evicted parent and child in the reject\nfilter until the next block, so a new child could not bump the parent\nback in.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Greg Sanders",
        "email": "gsanders87@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-09-24T15:57:48Z"
      },
      "author": {
        "name": "Greg Sanders",
        "email": "gsanders87@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-09-24T13:51:30Z"
